ict,1378.0,1478.0,2856.0,56122.6,unlikely_candidate,U,2,"This paper is a systematic review of asymptomatic and presymptomatic SARS-CoV-2 transmission. While it discusses serial interval literature, it does not present original empirical data or a new estimate of the serial interval or generation time, making it unsuitable as a primary source for the target parameter.",4,Explicitly investigates SARS-CoV-2 transmission dynamics.,4,Focuses on human clinical data and transmission studies.,3,"Systematic review covering multiple real-world settings globally, though no single location is specified.",1,Identified as a systematic review that synthesizes existing literature rather than reporting new primary data.,1,Includes serial interval studies in its review but does not calculate or report a new original estimate of the parameter.,0.9,,,,,,
