# Results

# Overview of epidemiology and clinical characteristics

Between 12 January and 21 February 2020, a total of 69 $( 8 6 . 3 \% )$ confirmed COVID-19 cases and 11 $( 1 3 . 7 \% )$ asymptomatic carriers were identified in Lu’an. The source of infection for 75 cases $( 9 3 . 8 \% )$ was identified by field investigation and traceback. As shown in Figure 2, the epidemic lasted almost 40 days, and the onset of illness peaked from 27 January to 6 February. All hospitalised cases were discharged before 4 March, with no deaths reported. Of the 80 cases, 52 $( 6 5 . 0 \% )$ ) were male and 28 $( 3 5 . 0 \% )$ were female. The median age was 40 years (range: 10 months to 77 years), with most cases $( 8 1 . 3 \% )$ aged between 20 and 60 years. Of the 69 confirmed cases, 39 $( 5 6 . 5 \% )$ had a fever as the initial symptom, and pneumonia was present in $8 9 . 9 \%$ of the patients on admission. Other symptoms such as cough $( 3 7 . 3 \% )$

