32417744,"Monitoring disease transmissibility of 2019 novel coronavirus disease in Zhejiang, China.","Chong KC, Cheng W, Zhao S, Ling F, Mohammad KN, Wang MH, Zee BCY, Wei L, Xiong X, Liu H, Wang J, Chen E.",Int J Infect Dis. 2020 Jul;96:128-130. doi: 10.1016/j.ijid.2020.04.036. Epub 2020 May 15.,Chong,International journal of infectious diseases : IJID : official publication of the International Society for Infectious Diseases,2020,2020/05/18,PMC7227576,,10.1016/j.ijid.2020.04.036,"Owing to the frequent travel connections between Wuhan and Zhejiang, Zhejiang was the third worst-affected province in China with 1,205 cases confirmed before 26 February 2020. The transmissibility of the 2019 novel coronavirus disease was monitored in Zhejiang, accounting for the transmissions from imported cases. Even though Zhejiang was one of the worst-affected provinces, an interruption of disease transmission (i.e. instantaneous reproduction numbers <1) was observed in early/mid-February after a comprehensive set of interventions combating the outbreak.",COVID-19; Reproduction number; Serial interval; Travel restriction; Zhejiang,,title_abstract,strict,1238.0,1622.0,2860.0,59108.0,possible_candidate,P,3,"The study analyzes empirical COVID-19 transmission data in Zhejiang, China, and lists serial interval as a keyword. However, the abstract primarily focuses on reproduction numbers and intervention impacts, making the reporting of serial interval or generation time uncertain without full-text review.",4,Explicitly investigates 2019 novel coronavirus disease (COVID-19) transmission.,4,Focuses on human cases and transmission dynamics in a defined population.,4,"Situated in a real-world geographic context (Zhejiang, China).",3,Reports empirical analysis of surveillance data to monitor disease transmissibility and reproduction numbers.,2,"Keywords list 'Serial interval', but the abstract focuses on reproduction numbers and interventions. It may report or use serial interval as an input,