# Close contacts

By Apr 3rd, a total of 4007 close contacts were quarantined, 186 were confirmed with SARS-CoV-2 infection, with an overall secondary attack rate of $4 . 6 \%$ $9 5 \%$ CI: 4.0–5.3). The secondary rate was higher among family members or relatives $1 5 . 6 \%$ , 111/714) than that among social contacts $( 2 . 2 \%$ , 75/3363) $\left( \chi ^ { 2 } = 2 3 9 . 8 5 2 \right.$ , $P < 0 . 0 0 1 _ { \cdot }$ ).

Among 441 close contact of HCWs, 32 were confirmed with SARS-CoV-2 infection, with an overall secondary attack rate of $7 . 3 \%$ , which was higher than that of non-HCWs’, with a secondary attack rate of $4 . 2 \%$ (154/3636) $\left( \chi ^ { 2 } = 8 . 2 4 3 \right.$ , $P = 0 . 0 0 4 _ { , }$ ).

