# Research Letter

# Serial interval distribution of SARS-CoV-2 infection in Brazil

Carlos A. Prete Jr $^{1}$ , MSc $^{1}$ , Lewis Buss, MD $^{2}$ , Amy Dighe, PhD $^{3}$ , Victor Bertollo Porto, PhD $^{4}$ , Darlan da Silva Candido, MSc $^{5}$ , Fábio Ghilardi, MD $^{2}$ , Oliver G. Pybus, PhD $^{5}$ , Wanderson K. de Oliveira, PhD $^{4,9}$ , Julio H. R. Croda, PhD $^{7,8}$ , Ester C. Sabino, PhD $^{2}$ , Nuno Rodrigues Faria, PhD $^{2,3,5}$ , Christl A. Donnelly, PhD $^{3,6}$  and Vitor H. Nascimento $^{1}$ , PhD $^{1}$

$^{1}$ Department of Electronic Systems Engineering, University of São Paulo, Av. Prof. Luciano Gualberto, trav. 3, n. 158, Cidade Universitaria, Sao Paulo, SP, 05508-900, Brazil,  $^{2}$ Instituto de Medicina Tropical, University of São Paulo, Av dr Enéas Carvalho de Aguiar 470, São Paulo, SP, Brazil,  $^{3}$ MRC Centre for Global Infectious Disease Analysis, Department of Infectious Disease Epidemiology, School of Public Health, Imperial College London, St Mary's Campus, Norfolk Place, London W2 1PG, UK,  $^{4}$ Secretariat of Health Surveillance, Department of Immunization and Communicable Diseases, Coordination of the National Immunizations Program, Brazilian Ministry of Health, Brazil,  $^{5}$ Department of Zoology, University of Oxford, Zoology Research and Administration Building, 11a Mansfield Road, Oxford OX1 3SZ, UK,  $^{6}$ Department of Statistics, University of Oxford, 24-29 St Giles, Oxford OX1 3LB, UK,  $^{7}$ Fundação Oswaldo Cruz, Mato Grosso do Sul Rua Gabriel Abrão, 92 - Jardim das Nações, Campo Grande - MS, 79074-460, Brazil,  $^{8}$ Faculdade de Medicina, Universidade Federal do Mato Grosso do Sul, Brazil and  $^{9}$ Hospital das Forças Armadas - Ministério da Defesa, Brazil

