# 3.5. Incubation period and serial interval

The median incubation period for 27 of the cases was 6 days (range, $1 { \cdot } 1 3 \mathrm { d }$ ; mean, 6.0 d; SD 3.1 d) (Fig. 2). The median serial interval for 31 of the cases was 4 days (range, $- 3 - 2 4 \mathrm { ~ d ~ }$ ; mean, 5.1 d; SD, 5.6 d) (Fig. 3). Two cases had negative serial intervals, and two cases had a zero-serial interval.

# 3.6. Infectious period

Twenty-six cases $( 4 7 . 3 \% )$ were infected in the presymptomatic period of the primary cases. Eleven cases $( 2 0 \% )$ were infected in

